        "original_id": "48b15dd9-a06b-598b-b46e-aa323473362f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Gorton, Harold Holt, Tony Eggleton, Robert Menzies, John McEwen, William McMahon\n- Roles: Prime Minister of Australia, press secretary\n- Organizations: University of Melbourne, Australian Film Institute\n- Events: 1969 Australian Film Institute Awards, Harold Holt's disappearance and death\n- Places: Stanmore, New South Wales\n\nFacts:\n- John Gorton was born on 9 September 1911 and died on 19 May 2002.\n- Harold Holt was born in Stanmore, New South Wales.\n- Harold Holt won a scholarship to study law at the University of Melbourne.\n- In December 1967, Tony Eggleton was the press secretary to Prime Minister of Australia Harold Holt at the time of Holt's disappearance and death.\n- John Gorton was the 19th Prime Minister of Australia.\n- John Gorton was a long-serving minister in the governments of Robert Menzies, Harold Holt, John McEwen, and William McMahon.\n- In 1969, Australian Prime Minister John Gorton hosted the 1969 Australian Film Institute Awards ceremony.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
